{
  "$schema_version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "description": "Normalized domain.operation view of datasets/intents.json for brain/router (hybrid semantic router). This file does NOT replace datasets/intents.json — it is a deliberate projection of a subset of it (only intents whose response_mode is 'skill' AND that are not already handled by a deterministic guard in brain/intent_engine.py). Conversational intents (smalltalk, identity, joke, motivate, opinion, followup, general_query, unknown) and guard-handled intents (dismissal, greet, farewell, thanks, help, perform_action) are intentionally excluded — they keep using their existing paths. The legacy 'mute' intent is likewise NOT projected here: there is no media.mute operation, and a bare mute/silence utterance falls through to the LLM fallback / legacy engine. Each operation's 'seeds' list holds its semantic prototypes: one stored vector per seed, aggregated per domain.operation at retrieval time. Add prototypes here, never in routing code; the same seed may not appear under two operations. If datasets/intents.json's keyword_rules_order, an intent id, or an intent's response_mode changes, this file must be reviewed for drift; brain/router/command_vector_store.py fingerprints this file (not datasets/intents.json) to decide when to reseed. Seed-writing rules: a seed must express the OPERATION (verb + object), not merely mention a shared noun (time/timer/clipboard/google/volume); contrastive pairs (create/status, read/copy/clear, pause/play, up/down, previous/next, date/time, search/open) must not share verbs or cue words that would make one seed plausible for both. A search-engine or site name used as a VERB before a topic ('google <topic>') is web.search; app_or_web.open holds only navigation to the site/app itself ('open google', 'go to google'). 'start'/'run'/'launch' only imply app_or_web.open when the object is an application, program, utility or destination. Playback-status questions ('what's playing') have no operation and must not be seeded under media.play.",
    "removed_operations": [
      "media.mute"
    ]
  },
